From bf1d7077c4417b5da1e07356a9e8c03b3d7d42c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ekkapot Charoenwanit <ekkapot.c@tggs.kmutnb.ac.th>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:15:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] get_total_partitions(), and lead the lorenz report with
 the two numbers

Asking how many partitions a tape was broken into required an
MPI_Allreduce over get_partitions(), which is per-rank.  It should not:
topmost_owner_idx is set at the end of the profiling pass, and the
profiling pass is IDENTICAL on every rank -- it builds no graph, only
counts, and the counting is a deterministic function of the operation
sequence.  So every rank has known the total since before the first
productive pass, and terminate() and the PASSES_COLLECTIVE branch both
already relied on precisely that.

boltzmann::get_total_partitions() hands it over.  No message, no
collective, zero before the profiling pass finishes -- same contract as
get_partitions(), which remains this rank's share of it.  MPI_size() was
already there for the rank count.

examples/lorenz now leads with both:

    lorenz: 148 partitions over 4 MPI ranks

rather than leaving them in the third field of the second line, and it
cross-checks the library's local number against the reduced sum of the
per-rank counts.  If those ever diverge, a rank recorded a partition
nobody scheduled or dropped one that was scheduled -- and the cheap
answer is the one everything else in the library trusts, so it is worth
an assertion rather than an assumption.

regress M-07 makes the same check a permanent one, at whatever rank
count the suite runs at, plus the no-tape case.  55 checks, up from 50.

Verified: seven pinned invariants bit-identical at 1, 2, 3, 4 ranks,
fdcheck 48/48, regress 55/55, whole suite green, clean under
AddressSanitizer and LeakSanitizer, zero library warnings.
